# Issue #5578's design, reproduced: the advance is armed by the born rule or by
# reaching the activation's first own append, and appends need no claim, so a
# stale duplicate keeps appending. Its acknowledged entry is passed, captured
# out of the shared snapshot and trimmed. Moved from the design's mutation of the
# same name; the epoch check it also removed is the environment's here, so the
# edit to OwnAlloc removes the current-activation constraint instead.
MODULE: NoTrimPastAckedLiveAdvance5578
TARGET: NoTrimPastAcked
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: #5578 exactly: arming by birth or by a read position within one of an own append, with no claim and no current-activation check
PERTURBS: OwnAlloc

--- FIND
Armed(a) ==
    /\ claimed[a]
    /\ mInit
    /\ IF WithPreArm THEN rp[a] >= seenP[a] ELSE rp[a] >= claimHead[a] - 1
    /\ ~pend
    /\ ~hoOpen
    /\ rp[a] >= hoClosedAt - 1
    /\ rp[a] >= seenU[a]
    /\ \A o \in inflight : author[o] # a
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: #5578's arming rule, with its applied-prefix tracker.
Armed(a) ==
    /\ a = "a1" \/ \E o \in mine[a] : rp[a] >= o - 1
    /\ \A o \in inflight : author[o] # a
--- END

--- FIND
    /\ a \in up
    /\ cur = a
    /\ next < MaxOff
--- REPLACE
    /\ a \in up
\* MUTATION: no claim; any running activation appends stamped.
    /\ next < MaxOff
--- END
